@startuml
' Drag fade handle -> video opacity preview and/or audio mix

actor User
participant TimelineView
participant TimelineEditor
participant "SetFade*Command" as Cmd
participant Clip
participant EditorViewModel
participant FrameCompositor
participant AudioMixer

User -> TimelineView : drag inner edge (fade zone)
activate TimelineView
TimelineView -> TimelineEditor : SetFadeIn / SetFadeOut(sec)
activate TimelineEditor
TimelineEditor -> Cmd : ExecuteCoalescing (whole link group)
activate Cmd
Cmd -> Clip : FadeInSec / FadeOutSec = clamped
deactivate Cmd
TimelineEditor --> TimelineView
deactivate TimelineEditor
TimelineView -> TimelineView : redraw fade ramp
deactivate TimelineView

... video scrub / play ...

EditorViewModel -> Clip : Fade* + Opacity
EditorViewModel -> FrameCompositor : opacity = Opacity * envelope

... audio play ...

AudioMixer -> Clip : Fade* + Volume
AudioMixer -> AudioMixer : per-frame gain = Volume * envelope

note over TimelineView
  Outer ~6px = trim.
  Inner zone = FadeIn / FadeOut.
  Works on video and audio clips.
end note

note over Cmd
  Link group gets the same fade
  durations (A/V stay in sync).
end note

@enduml
